-- title:
--   Descent of a Frobenius-invariant family to the fixed subalgebra
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$. Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain that is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi\in\mathcal O$ irreducible, $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic filtration, with $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ and every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (so the residue ring is an algebraic closure of $\mathcal O/\pi$), and let $Fr$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$ with $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$. Fix $m>0$, a functor $Y$ on $\mathcal O$-algebras (in the project's sense: an assignment $B\mapsto Y(B)$ with functorial transport along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps), a scheme $T$ and a morphism $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Suppose given, for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map $\rho_B:(Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times Y(B)\to\{\varphi:\operatorname{Spec}B\to T \mid t\circ\varphi=\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O\to B)\}$, natural in $B$, and invariant under twisting, $\rho_B(\psi\circ Fr^{m},y)=\rho_B(\psi,y)$. Then there is a family $\bar\rho$ of the same shape with $Onr$ replaced by the subalgebra $\{x\in Onr: Fr^{m}x=x\}$, natural in $B$, with $\rho_B(\psi,y)=\bar\rho_B(\psi|_{\{Fr^m=\mathrm{id}\}},y)$; and any natural $\bar\rho'$ with the same factorisation property agrees with $\bar\rho$ at every such $B$ and every argument.
--
--   This is the scalar-descent step along the unramified extension in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: a family of $T$-valued points parametrised by $\mathcal O$-embeddings of the completed unramified base, invariant under the $m$-th power of the Frobenius, descends uniquely to a family parametrised by embeddings of the degree-$m$ unramified subring. It is used in the variant for the square of the Frobenius and in the comparison statements for fine moduli problems over $T$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_existsUnique_factor_corep_fixedPoints_of_frobTwist_eq.lean

